    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a stiff challenge today against Henderson, whose 3.13 xERA necessitates a conservative outlook across our offensive stack. **Kyle Tucker** emerges as our primary offensive engine with a score of 47.89. While his placement in the #8 hole dampens his counting stat potential, his elite base-scoring projection remains the anchor of the lineup; we are banking on his professional approach to neutralize the high-skill profile of the opposing starter. **Andy Pages** follows in the UTIL spot at 42.21, functioning as a marginal start. Despite the neutral platoon advantage, the decision to play **Andy Pages** is driven by his proximity to the floor; we are monitoring his ability to generate momentum against a pitcher who limits free-base opportunities.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 34.01. His exclusion is primarily a function of the \"Zebras\" 40.0 floor rule, designed to protect our game-cap allocation during tough matchups. The combination of a high-skill opponent in Henderson and a bottom-of-the-order assignment suppressed his viability despite his speed profile. Looking ahead, we continue to manage the absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, the latter of whom remains sidelined on the IL. With no immediate reinforcements available from the bench, our priority remains the preservation of daily efficiency while waiting for more favorable matchups for depth pieces like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, or **Heliot Ramos**. We remain disciplined; we will not burn cap room on players falling below our established efficiency thresholds in low-probability games.",
